{"type":"new","contents":"import Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card\nimport Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic\n\n/-!\n# Prime A1 Root System\n\nA Mathlib-rooted finite `A₁^P` root-system core.  The only primitive datum is a\nfinite set of natural numbers together with Mathlib `Nat.Prime` evidence for\neach member.  Weyl elements are finite subsets of that subtype, so every Weyl\ncoordinate carries its prime certificate back to `Nat.Prime` without external\nnumber-theoretic assumptions.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Algebra\n\n/-- A finite set of primes defining a cutoff `A₁^P` root system. -/\nstructure PrimeA1RootSystem where\n  P : Finset ℕ\n  all_prime : ∀ p ∈ P, Nat.Prime p\n\nnamespace PrimeA1RootSystem\n\n/-- The Weyl group of the finite `A₁^P` system is the Boolean group of subsets of `P`. -/\nabbrev WeylGroup (S : PrimeA1RootSystem) := Finset (S.P)\n\n/-- The signature of a Weyl group element is `(-1) ^ |w|`. -/\ndef signature {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} (w : S.WeylGroup) : ℤ :=\n  if w.card % 2 = 0 then 1 else -1\n\n/-- Forget subtype coordinates of a Weyl element back to the ambient prime cutoff. -/\ndef support {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} (w : S.WeylGroup) : Finset ℕ :=\n  w.image Subtype.val\n\n/-- Read back the Mathlib primality certificate for an ambient element of `P`. -/\ntheorem prime_of_mem (S : PrimeA1RootSystem) {p : ℕ} (hp : p ∈ S.P) : Nat.Prime p :=\n  S.all_prime p hp\n\n/-- Read back the Mathlib primality certificate carried by a Weyl coordinate. -/\ntheorem prime_of_weyl_coord {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} (p : S.P) : Nat.Prime p.1 :=\n  S.prime_of_mem p.2\n\n/-- Membership in a Weyl element is still membership in the prime cutoff. -/\ntheorem mem_cutoff_of_mem_weyl {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} {w : S.WeylGroup} {p : S.P}\n    (_hp : p ∈ w) : p.1 ∈ S.P :=\n  p.2\n\n/-- A Weyl coordinate selected by a Weyl element is prime. -/\ntheorem prime_of_mem_weyl {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} {w : S.WeylGroup} {p : S.P}\n    (_hp : p ∈ w) : Nat.Prime p.1 :=\n  S.prime_of_weyl_coord p\n\n/-- The ambient support of a Weyl element lies inside the prime cutoff. -/\ntheorem support_subset {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} {w : S.WeylGroup} :\n    support w ⊆ S.P := by\n  classical\n  intro p hp\n  rcases Finset.mem_image.mp hp with ⟨q, _hqw, hq⟩\n  rw [← hq]\n  exact q.2\n\n/-- Every ambient coordinate in a Weyl support has Mathlib primality evidence. -/\ntheorem prime_of_mem_support {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} {w : S.WeylGroup} {p : ℕ}\n    (hp : p ∈ support w) : Nat.Prime p :=\n  S.prime_of_mem (support_subset hp)\n\n@[simp] theorem support_empty (S : PrimeA1RootSystem) :\n    support (S := S) (∅ : S.WeylGroup) = ∅ := by\n  simp [support]\n\n@[simp] theorem signature_of_even {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} {w : S.WeylGroup}\n    (h : w.card % 2 = 0) : signature w = 1 := by\n  simp [signature, h]\n\n@[simp] theorem signature_of_odd {S : PrimeA1RootSystem} {w : S.WeylGroup}\n    (h : w.card % 2 ≠ 0) : signature w = -1 := by\n  simp [signature, h]\n\nend PrimeA1RootSystem\n\nend InfoGeometry.Algebra\n","mtime":1778324301307}